# Architecture

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture/` before implementing features.
- Modular monolith only: domain modules + shared kernel; no microservices split.
- Stack lock: Next.js App Router, Supabase (Auth/Postgres/Storage/RLS), Dexie offline — see ADRs 0001–0002.
- Separate **templates/plans** from **performed sessions/logs** always.
- Domains in scope: nutrition, workouts, rehab, hydration, meditation, measurements, progress photos, calendar, profile, custom trackers.
- Out of scope: feeds, social, general journaling; Odiina is a separate app.
- Follow `BUILD_INCREMENTS.md`; do not start the next increment without user approval.
- Prefer documenting decisions in ADRs over silent stack changes.
- Motion preference in code: `full` | `reduced` | `off` (`disabled` in older docs maps to `off`).
